  { q: 'What is a group of ravens called?', a: 'A group of ravens has several collective nouns: the most widely used are "an unkindness of ravens" (derived from the Book of Saint Albans, 1486) and "a conspiracy of ravens." In practice, ornithologists simply describe "a flock" or "a roost" of ravens — the terms of venery are literary rather than scientific. See the full page on collective nouns for ravens.' },
